{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-24 13:13:47 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-24 20:13:47 +07\n\n**Deferred-grant lifecycle defect — resolved.** `src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc:114` leaves the fact cursor unchanged until the reading is usable. Once usable, `:120–133` folds grants and subsequent lapses in medium order before returning control. `holding?` at `:148` rejects the resulting lapsed holder. Pending storage has been removed.\n\nThe regression test at `test/dao/star/r5_test.clj:12` covers deferred grant → lapse → usable reading and checks no holding, renewal, or projection. The foreign-grant test and implementation confirm that rejected grants no longer accumulate locally.\n\n**Duplicated validation — acceptable, nonblocking.** `usable-reading?` at `src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc:79` currently matches `dao.lease`’s private `reading-ok?` at `src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc:1720`: duration shape, known unit, and per-unit magnitude bound. Both use the public duration predicate and magnitude limit. Future consolidation would reduce drift risk, but does not justify crossing the stated ownership boundary for this fix.\n\n**New defects:** none identified in the r5 change or its interactions with the previously reviewed projection and gap handling. Existing host-support limitations remain as previously recorded.\n\nRead-only review completed; no suites rerun. Validation relies on the orchestrator’s supplied results.\n\n**SIGNED OFF**"}}
